What was not carried
--------------------

  linux_voice_assistant/__main__.py
      The command-line entry point: argument parsing, logging setup, device
      enumeration and process wiring. This application is started by the Reachy
      Mini daemon, not from a shell, so none of it applies.

  linux_voice_assistant/mpv_player.py
  linux_voice_assistant/player/
      The media-player playback path, which drives an `mpv` subprocess. On this
      robot the daemon owns the speaker. Replaced by the `MediaPlayback` seam.

  The desktop capture path (`soundcard`, inside `__main__.py`)
      The daemon owns the microphone array. Replaced by the `AudioCapture` seam.

  tests/unit/test_main.py, tests/unit/test_mpv_player.py
      They cover only the code above.

  Everything else in the upstream repository — its packaging, container images,
  documentation, examples and continuous integration.

What was changed
----------------

The intent is that the diff from upstream stays small, deliberate and
enumerable. It is:

1. Each file gained the provenance header described above.

2. `entity.py` and `models.py` take `seams.MediaPlayback` where upstream took
   `mpv_player.MpvMediaPlayer`. The seam is that class's public surface and
   nothing more, so no call site changed.

3. `models.ServerState` gained one optional field, `audio_capture`, typed
   `seams.AudioCapture`. It is where the capture the discarded entry point
   performed is reached from instead.

4. `wake_word.py` lost a `#!/usr/bin/env python3` shebang it did not use; the
   module is imported, never executed.

5. The carried tests import from this package rather than from
   `linux_voice_assistant`, were renamed so their module names are unique across
   the repository, and run against an in-memory filesystem — this repository
   requires that a unit test perform no input or output, and upstream's tests
   wrote preference files and wake-word configurations to real temporary
   directories. The change is one fixture in `conftest.py`; no test body was
   rewritten. Two upstream test files were dropped entirely, listed above.

6. Example addresses use the RFC 5737 documentation ranges: in the carried
   tests, and in one comment in `util.py` illustrating what `netifaces` returns.
   This repository is public and requires that of every tracked file.

7. Two of upstream's type-check suppressions gained the error code they were
   missing, in `util.py` and `peripheral_api.py`. This repository runs mypy with
   `ignore-without-code`, so a blanket `# type: ignore` is an error rather than a
   style preference, and the relaxation these modules carry deliberately does not
   extend to it: a suppression naming what it suppresses is the one rule worth
   keeping even here.

Nothing else was touched. In particular the code is not reformatted, its
docstrings are not rewritten, and its typing is not modernised — the shared ruff
and mypy configuration names these files and stands down, which is why the
diff above is the whole diff.

Neither seam is implemented here. Change 0012 supplies the daemon-backed
adapters; until then this package imports, and its carried tests pass, with both
holes open.

Assets
------

The wake-word models and sounds that ship in the wheel come from the same
upstream repository but are not code and do not live here. They are in
`../assets/`, with their own notice and a registry recording each one's source
and licence.
